  <main>
    <p>Welcome to my color gallery! This site showcases a simple grid of colors, each represented by an image and a short caption. It was built to practice responsive web design using CSS Grid and media queries.</p>

    <p>As you resize the browser window, notice how the layout adapts: a single column on mobile devices, two columns on tablets with circular images, and a slightly different two-column layout on larger desktop screens. The site also supports a dark color scheme and respects reduced motion preferences.</p>

    <div class = "grid">
        <figure>
        <img src="images/Red.jpeg" alt="Red" width="200">
        <figcaption class="label">Red</figcaption>
        </figure>
        <figure>
        <img src="images/Orange.png" alt="Orange" width="200">
        <figcaption class="label">Orange</figcaption>
        </figure>
        <figure>
        <img src="images/Yellow.png" alt="Yellow" width="200">
        <figcaption class="label">Yellow</figcaption>
        </figure>
        <figure>
        <img src="images/Green.png" alt="Green" width="200">
        <figcaption class="label">Green</figcaption>
        </figure>
        <figure>
        <img src="images/Blue.png" alt="Blue" width="200">
        <figcaption class="label">Blue</figcaption>
        </figure>
        <figure>
        <img src="images/Indigo.jpeg" alt="Indigo" width="200">
        <figcaption class="label">Indigo</figcaption>
        </figure>
        <figure>
        <img src="images/Purple.png" alt="Purple" width="200">
        <figcaption class="label">Purple</figcaption>
        </figure>
        <figure>
        <img src="images/Pink.jpeg" alt="Pink" width="200">
        <figcaption class="label">Pink</figcaption>
        </figure>
        <figure>
        <img src="images/White.png" alt="White" width="200">
        <figcaption class="label">White</figcaption>
        </figure>
    </div>
  </main>

  <footer>
    <a href="#top">Jump to the Top</a>
  </footer>
</body>

</html>